cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this work, please cite the paper you rely on. The Stage 3 preprint below is the citation with a DOI; the synthesis paper is the overview of the whole programme."
title: "FRM: Felix Runtime Module — papers and results"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Felix
    given-names: Junai P.
    email: junai.felixx@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Taipei, Taiwan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-1641-0399"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/recurse-root/FRMDevelopment"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23366848"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23366848"
    description: "Concept DOI for all archived releases of this repository"
abstract: >-
  Papers and results for FRM, the Felix Runtime Module, a bounded
  self-improving program-repair system tested in nine preregistered studies
  against a published Level-4 definition of recursive self-improvement. The
  repository holds the synthesis of the programme, the Stage 3 (FELIX-C3)
  Level-4 test, the FELIX-C7 real-bug transfer study, the FELIX-C9 study of
  structural self-modification, per-seed result tables with a script that
  recomputes the reported statistics, a registered follow-up test (T1) with
  its results, and an earlier preprint on the FELIX v4 self-evolving organism.
keywords:
  - recursive self-improvement
  - self-referential improvement
  - capability taxonomy
  - autonomous operation
  - preregistration
  - automated program repair
  - external validity
  - self-modification
  - generalisation
